Package: placeindex
Title: Residential Concentration, Spatial Access and Composite Indices
    for Places
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Zachary Lorico", "Hertz", , "zachary_hertz@berkeley.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds decennial census block data assigned to places,
    measures how concentrated a group is within each place (dissimilarity,
    isolation, exposure, and contiguous clusters of majority-group blocks),
    measures spatial access to sites with limited capacity with the
    enhanced two-step floating catchment area method, and combines
    indicators into composite indices with a Monte Carlo
    analysis of how ranks depend on construction choices. Validation
    helpers aggregate unit scores to the units a survey identifies and
    extract shrunken group effects from multilevel models.
